1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,002
They say,

2
00:00:01,002 --> 00:00:07,016
the shadow of the Tanjore temple never falls on the ground at noon.

3
00:00:07,016 --> 00:00:12,027
Some people call it a miracle, some call it just a story.

4
00:00:12,027 --> 00:00:15,034
The truth is hidden somewhere in between.

5
00:00:15,034 --> 00:00:19,043
In this video we will look at the evidence,

6
00:00:19,043 --> 00:00:22,050
and find out where the shadow actually goes.

7
00:00:22,050 --> 00:00:24,853
And a bigger question than the shadow,

8
00:00:24,853 --> 00:00:29,993
the stone placed at the very top of the temple. ASI records say,

9
00:00:29,993 --> 00:00:33,730
under the dome there is a single block of granite.

10
00:00:33,730 --> 00:00:38,870
Its weight is said to be around 80 tons. There was no crane,

11
00:00:38,870 --> 00:00:42,140
no truck, so how did it get up there?

12
00:00:42,140 --> 00:00:47,532
Even today, grandmothers in villages tell this story to children.

13
00:00:47,532 --> 00:00:52,435
That the king built a temple that never bends,

14
00:00:52,435 --> 00:00:57,827
never breaks. But the grandmother's story and the ASI report

15
00:00:57,827 --> 00:00:59,788
are not always the same.

16
00:00:59,788 --> 00:01:03,710
So we will put a clear label on every claim.

17
00:01:03,710 --> 00:01:07,945
On every panel you will see a small chip.

18
00:01:07,945 --> 00:01:12,708
Legend means a famous story with no written proof.

19
00:01:12,708 --> 00:01:18,002
Archaeology means an institution went there itself, looked, and recorded it.

20
00:01:18,002 --> 00:01:22,236
Disputed means experts do not agree with each other. Come,

21
00:01:22,236 --> 00:01:27,000
first let us hear the story, the way people have been telling it.

22
00:01:27,000 --> 00:01:30,853
The story begins in the delta of the Kaveri river,

23
00:01:30,853 --> 00:01:33,422
where the Chola kings ruled.

24
00:01:33,422 --> 00:01:35,991
Delta means the part of a river

25
00:01:35,991 --> 00:01:40,272
where it spreads out before meeting the sea.

26
00:01:40,272 --> 00:01:42,413
The land here was fertile,

27
00:01:42,413 --> 00:01:45,410
and the king's dream was very big.

28
00:01:45,410 --> 00:01:50,612
According to ASI, this temple was built by Rajaraja Chola.

29
00:01:50,612 --> 00:01:55,815
Inside the temple is a Shivling, and above it a vimana touching the sky.

30
00:01:55,815 --> 00:02:01,537
Vimana means the tall tower, like stairs, rising above the sanctum.

31
00:02:01,537 --> 00:02:05,699
Sanctum means the innermost room of the temple,

32
00:02:05,699 --> 00:02:07,780
where worship is done.

33
00:02:07,780 --> 00:02:12,673
Now come the stories that every guide tells.

34
00:02:12,673 --> 00:02:14,141
The most famous story:

35
00:02:14,141 --> 00:02:19,034
at noon, the shadow of this vimana does not fall on the ground.

36
00:02:19,034 --> 00:02:24,417
People say the Chola craftsmen even outdid the sun.

37
00:02:24,417 --> 00:02:29,310
But no old written proof of this is found.

38
00:02:29,310 --> 00:02:30,202
The next story:

39
00:02:30,202 --> 00:02:35,555
the heavy stone at the top was taken up along a very long earth ramp.

40
00:02:35,555 --> 00:02:40,909
They say this ramp started from a place called Sarapallam.

41
00:02:40,909 --> 00:02:45,816
Elephants and bulls kept pulling the stones, day after day,

42
00:02:45,816 --> 00:02:47,600
month after month.

43
00:02:47,600 --> 00:02:49,236
And the last story:

44
00:02:49,236 --> 00:02:54,144
no crack has ever appeared in this temple.

45
00:02:54,144 --> 00:02:59,598
A crack means a thin split in a wall or a stone.

46
00:02:59,598 --> 00:03:02,870
People say that centuries of rain,

47
00:03:02,870 --> 00:03:07,233
sun and earthquakes could not shake it either.

48
00:03:07,233 --> 00:03:11,050
This sounds wonderful to hear.

49
00:03:11,050 --> 00:03:14,876
So the stories are in front of us: the shadow, the slope and the crack.

50
00:03:14,876 --> 00:03:19,181
Now the question is how much of it is true.

51
00:03:19,181 --> 00:03:23,007
For that, we have to go beyond the storytellers

52
00:03:23,007 --> 00:03:27,312
and go to the people who measure. Let's see

53
00:03:27,312 --> 00:03:30,660
what the ASI and UNESCO have written.

54
00:03:30,660 --> 00:03:33,118
According to ASI records,

55
00:03:33,118 --> 00:03:38,527
the temple was completed around 1010 CE. CE means common era,

56
00:03:38,527 --> 00:03:43,935
the same year count we use on the calendar.

57
00:03:43,935 --> 00:03:46,885
The king himself inaugurated it,

58
00:03:46,885 --> 00:03:51,310
and named it Rajesvara Peruvudaiyar after himself.

59
00:03:51,310 --> 00:03:54,153
How did this information reach us?

60
00:03:54,153 --> 00:03:57,944
Through the inscriptions carved on the temple walls.

61
00:03:57,944 --> 00:04:01,735
Inscriptions are old records written on stone.

62
00:04:01,735 --> 00:04:07,421
They mention the king's donations and the work done on the temple.

63
00:04:07,421 --> 00:04:12,160
These are called the Thanjavur inscriptions, think of them as a diary in stone.

64
00:04:12,160 --> 00:04:18,603
UNESCO has placed this temple in the group called Great Living Chola Temples.

65
00:04:18,603 --> 00:04:23,327
Living means a temple where worship still happens every day.

66
00:04:23,327 --> 00:04:27,193
That means this is not a closed museum, it is a working temple.

67
00:04:27,193 --> 00:04:29,770
And the ASI looks after it.

68
00:04:29,770 --> 00:04:32,253
Now let's talk about the stone.

69
00:04:32,253 --> 00:04:34,736
The whole temple is made of granite,

70
00:04:34,736 --> 00:04:37,220
which is a very hard stone.

71
00:04:37,220 --> 00:04:41,772
Granite is the stone you see in kitchen slabs,

72
00:04:41,772 --> 00:04:43,428
which is hard to cut.

73
00:04:43,428 --> 00:04:47,980
And these heavy blocks were brought across the Kaveri delta.

74
00:04:47,980 --> 00:04:53,877
Right on top of the vimana is a dome, called the shikhara.

75
00:04:53,877 --> 00:04:57,629
According to the ASI, this shikhara is octagonal,

76
00:04:57,629 --> 00:05:01,381
just like the shape of a traffic stop sign.

77
00:05:01,381 --> 00:05:04,597
And this dome rests on a single granite

78
00:05:04,597 --> 00:05:09,422
square block. Square means

79
00:05:09,422 --> 00:05:11,030
having equal sides.

80
00:05:11,030 --> 00:05:15,300
The ASI says the weight of this very square block is very heavy,

81
00:05:15,300 --> 00:05:18,405
as many as several elephants. And lifting it off the ground,

82
00:05:18,405 --> 00:05:22,674
it had to be taken to the top of the vimana. Without any motor,

83
00:05:22,674 --> 00:05:24,227
without any crane.

84
00:05:24,227 --> 00:05:27,720
This is the biggest engineering question of this temple.

85
00:05:27,720 --> 00:05:32,726
Now the next important thing: there is no mortar between these stones.

86
00:05:32,726 --> 00:05:36,822
Mortar means the paste that joins bricks together.

87
00:05:36,822 --> 00:05:39,553
The Chola craftsmen cut the stones in such a way

88
00:05:39,553 --> 00:05:43,194
that they lock into each other and join.

89
00:05:43,194 --> 00:05:47,290
This is called interlocking, just like Lego pieces.

90
00:05:47,290 --> 00:05:52,188
This interlocking is believed to be the secret of the temple's strength.

91
00:05:52,188 --> 00:05:57,575
When an earthquake comes, the stones shift a little, but they don't fall apart.

92
00:05:57,575 --> 00:06:01,494
Like a chair made of tightly fitted wooden joints,

93
00:06:01,494 --> 00:06:04,432
it takes a shove but doesn't fall.

94
00:06:04,432 --> 00:06:09,820
Researchers link this flexibility to the temple's long life.

95
00:06:09,820 --> 00:06:12,440
So what about the story of no cracks?

96
00:06:12,440 --> 00:06:16,371
Every stone building wears down with time,

97
00:06:16,371 --> 00:06:18,118
this is what science says.

98
00:06:18,118 --> 00:06:22,485
But the structure of this temple still stands strong today,

99
00:06:22,485 --> 00:06:25,979
this is true. And that there has never been any crack,

100
00:06:25,979 --> 00:06:29,910
this claim is not written like that in any report.

101
00:06:29,910 --> 00:06:33,680
Now let's come to the most famous claim, the shadow.

102
00:06:33,680 --> 00:06:37,450
The answer to this question is not in any book,

103
00:06:37,450 --> 00:06:42,634
it is right there in the sky. It needs a little geometry, but don't worry.

104
00:06:42,634 --> 00:06:45,461
I will keep it as simple

105
00:06:45,461 --> 00:06:48,760
as watching the sunlight while standing on a rooftop.

106
00:06:48,760 --> 00:06:51,290
First, understand how a shadow is formed.

107
00:06:51,290 --> 00:06:54,664
Sunlight travels in a straight line.

108
00:06:54,664 --> 00:06:58,881
Whatever comes in the middle, the light doesn't reach behind it.

109
00:06:58,881 --> 00:07:03,520
That dark part is the shadow. The lower the sun, the longer the shadow.

110
00:07:03,520 --> 00:07:06,050
The higher the sun, the shorter the shadow.

111
00:07:06,050 --> 00:07:09,138
In the morning and evening the sun is low,

112
00:07:09,138 --> 00:07:13,109
so the vimana's long shadow falls far away.

113
00:07:13,109 --> 00:07:16,638
You can go there and see this yourself.

114
00:07:16,638 --> 00:07:21,050
It means the temple casts a shadow, just like other buildings.

115
00:07:21,050 --> 00:07:25,020
There is no magic here, it's simply the play of the sun.

116
00:07:25,020 --> 00:07:27,132
Now think about the afternoon.

117
00:07:27,132 --> 00:07:30,089
The sun is almost right overhead.

118
00:07:30,089 --> 00:07:36,004
Then the shadow of everything shrinks and comes near its feet.

119
00:07:36,004 --> 00:07:41,073
Like at noon your shadow hides under your shoes.

120
00:07:41,073 --> 00:07:44,030
The same happens with the temple.

121
00:07:44,030 --> 00:07:49,474
Now look at the twist. The vimana doesn't rise straight from the ground. It stands on a wide,

122
00:07:49,474 --> 00:07:52,443
stepped base.

123
00:07:52,443 --> 00:07:55,412
A plinth means that high, wide platform

124
00:07:55,412 --> 00:07:58,381
on which the building rests.

125
00:07:58,381 --> 00:08:02,835
And as the vimana goes up, it gets narrower,

126
00:08:02,835 --> 00:08:04,320
like a pyramid.

127
00:08:04,320 --> 00:08:07,529
So where does the short noon shadow fall?

128
00:08:07,529 --> 00:08:10,337
Right on the temple's own wide plinth.

129
00:08:10,337 --> 00:08:12,343
Before it reaches the ground,

130
00:08:12,343 --> 00:08:15,953
it gets absorbed into the temple's own stone.

131
00:08:15,953 --> 00:08:19,964
To the man standing below, it looks like the shadow has vanished.

132
00:08:19,964 --> 00:08:21,970
In reality, it is right there.

133
00:08:21,970 --> 00:08:27,242
So saying 'there is no shadow' is only half the truth. The shadow does form,

134
00:08:27,242 --> 00:08:31,555
it just isn't visible outside the temple at noon.

135
00:08:31,555 --> 00:08:35,869
And this is also proof of the craftsmen's understanding,

136
00:08:35,869 --> 00:08:39,703
a wide base and a narrowing tower. Not a miracle,

137
00:08:39,703 --> 00:08:41,620
but certainly a marvel.

138
00:08:41,620 --> 00:08:46,311
Now the question on which even the experts don't agree with each other.

139
00:08:46,311 --> 00:08:51,470
The big question: is the dome on top really a single stone?

140
00:08:51,470 --> 00:08:53,347
In the words of the ASI,

141
00:08:53,347 --> 00:08:57,099
the shikhara rests on a single block of granite.

142
00:08:57,099 --> 00:09:01,790
But some scholars say the story is not that simple.

143
00:09:01,790 --> 00:09:05,776
Some engineers believe it is a monolith.

144
00:09:05,776 --> 00:09:10,205
A monolith means one whole stone, with no joints.

145
00:09:10,205 --> 00:09:14,191
Others say it was made by cutting several stones

146
00:09:14,191 --> 00:09:18,177
and joining them so neatly that it looks like one.

147
00:09:18,177 --> 00:09:21,720
Without checking it up close, it is hard to decide.

148
00:09:21,720 --> 00:09:25,047
Now the question of the ramp. A ramp means a slope,

149
00:09:25,047 --> 00:09:28,849
like the sloping path for wheelchairs in a building.

150
00:09:28,849 --> 00:09:32,651
The old story says a very long, straight ramp of earth

151
00:09:32,651 --> 00:09:35,502
was built from Sarapallam.

152
00:09:35,502 --> 00:09:40,730
Elephants and bullocks dragged the stone up it.

153
00:09:40,730 --> 00:09:46,667
But some scholars and engineers question this straight ramp.

154
00:09:46,667 --> 00:09:48,152
Their question is,

155
00:09:48,152 --> 00:09:53,099
how was such a long ramp built, and how was it removed afterwards?

156
00:09:53,099 --> 00:09:57,552
That is why some people talk about a spiral ramp.

157
00:09:57,552 --> 00:10:02,500
Spiral means a ramp winding around the temple, like a hill road.

158
00:10:02,500 --> 00:10:07,762
Those for the straight ramp say a long ramp gives a gentle climb,

159
00:10:07,762 --> 00:10:11,111
so pulling is easier. Those for the spiral say,

160
00:10:11,111 --> 00:10:13,981
a winding ramp takes up less space,

161
00:10:13,981 --> 00:10:19,243
and it rises up along with the temple. There are arguments on every side.

162
00:10:19,243 --> 00:10:23,070
But nobody has a written plan.

163
00:10:23,070 --> 00:10:27,913
And the Sarapallam story? People still take this name even today,

164
00:10:27,913 --> 00:10:31,434
but we could not find any old written record of it.

165
00:10:31,434 --> 00:10:36,277
So we will call it a legend only. It may be true,

166
00:10:36,277 --> 00:10:41,119
it may be a story added later. Until proof comes,

167
00:10:41,119 --> 00:10:42,440
the question stays open.

168
00:10:42,440 --> 00:10:44,506
Now the biggest gap.

169
00:10:44,506 --> 00:10:49,671
How was the heavy granite brought across the Kaveri delta? By boat,

170
00:10:49,671 --> 00:10:55,353
rope, or wooden rollers? Rollers means round wooden logs,

171
00:10:55,353 --> 00:10:58,968
on which heavy things are rolled along.

172
00:10:58,968 --> 00:11:04,650
In the records of that time, this method is simply not written.

173
00:11:04,650 --> 00:11:08,406
How many workers were used, in what order the work was done,

174
00:11:08,406 --> 00:11:12,163
where the stones were kept, even this is not clear.

175
00:11:12,163 --> 00:11:14,041
This is called staging,

176
00:11:14,041 --> 00:11:18,267
which means dividing a big job into parts and doing it step by step.

177
00:11:18,267 --> 00:11:22,493
For such a big job, this planning must have been done.

178
00:11:22,493 --> 00:11:25,780
But that paper has not been found yet.

179
00:11:25,780 --> 00:11:27,947
Being an accountant,

180
00:11:27,947 --> 00:11:33,906
what surprises me most is the planning. Such a huge job,

181
00:11:33,906 --> 00:11:39,323
without a computer, without a spreadsheet. Someone must have kept the accounts,

182
00:11:39,323 --> 00:11:44,740
of the stone, the workers, the food. If that account is found,

183
00:11:44,740 --> 00:11:47,990
a very big mystery would be solved.

184
00:11:47,990 --> 00:11:51,520
Even today this temple stands in Thanjavur,

185
00:11:51,520 --> 00:11:53,725
and worship happens every day.

186
00:11:53,725 --> 00:11:58,137
People also call it the Big Temple or Periya Kovil.

187
00:11:58,137 --> 00:12:02,549
Going inside, you can see the vimana from below.

188
00:12:02,549 --> 00:12:06,520
You have to tilt your head back, it looks that tall.

189
00:12:06,520 --> 00:12:11,410
If you go there, check the shadow yourself in the morning and at noon.

190
00:12:11,410 --> 00:12:16,790
In the morning, see the long shadow; at noon, see it gather close to the plinth.

191
00:12:16,790 --> 00:12:20,702
Also look carefully at the inscriptions carved on the walls.

192
00:12:20,702 --> 00:12:23,636
This is that diary in stone,

193
00:12:23,636 --> 00:12:26,570
from which we got the date 1010.

194
00:12:26,570 --> 00:12:28,785
Walk around the temple courtyard,

195
00:12:28,785 --> 00:12:31,886
and look carefully at the granite joints.

196
00:12:31,886 --> 00:12:35,430
In many places the stones are joined so neatly,

197
00:12:35,430 --> 00:12:39,861
that the line is hardly visible. Right here you will understand

198
00:12:39,861 --> 00:12:42,076
what interlocking means.

199
00:12:42,076 --> 00:12:45,620
And the question about the shikhara will feel even deeper.

200
00:12:45,620 --> 00:12:49,095
So the calculation is clear. The shadow forms,

201
00:12:49,095 --> 00:12:53,563
It only shrinks down to the temple at noon.

202
00:12:53,563 --> 00:12:58,527
The heavy stone on top is real, but how it got there

203
00:12:58,527 --> 00:13:03,988
is still a mystery. And the story of the Sarapallam ramp

204
00:13:03,988 --> 00:13:06,470
is still just a story.

205
00:13:06,470 --> 00:13:10,342
Now, a question for you. What do you think,

206
00:13:10,342 --> 00:13:15,873
did the stone go up a straight ramp, or a spiral ramp?

207
00:13:15,873 --> 00:13:19,744
Just write in the comments: straight or spiral.

208
00:13:19,744 --> 00:13:25,828
Next time we will head to the stone chariot of Hampi,

209
00:13:25,828 --> 00:13:29,700
where a new mystery is waiting.
